## Architecture (`{{architecture}}`)

{{#if (eq architecture "clean")}}
```text
lib/src/
├── features/<feature>/
│   ├── data/          # datasources, models, repository impls
│   ├── domain/        # entities, repo contracts, use cases
│   └── presentation/  # screens, widgets, state ({{stateManagement}})
├── routing/
├── services/
├── shared/
└── theme/
```

**Rules**

- `domain/` is pure Dart — no Flutter imports, no imports from `data/`.
- `data/` implements contracts from `domain/` — never the reverse.
- Prefer `UserModel` (data) for JSON; map to `AppUser` via `toEntity()`. Entity factories like `empty()` / `fromJson` are for convenience at boundaries.
- Use cases implement `UseCase<Params, Result>` with a single `call()` — see `domain/usecases/`.
- Remote IO goes through abstract datasources (`AuthRemoteDataSource`) that repositories depend on.
- `presentation/` talks to use cases or repositories — not datasources directly.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq architecture "feature-first")}}
```text
lib/src/
├── features/<feature>/
│   ├── data/          # datasources, models, repository impls
│   ├── domain/        # entities, repo contracts, use cases
│   └── presentation/  # screens, widgets, state ({{stateManagement}})
├── shared/            # cross-feature widgets & utils only
├── routing/
├── services/
└── theme/
```

**Rules**

- Each feature is self-contained — no imports from another feature's internals.
- Shared code lives only under `lib/src/shared/`.
- Same domain/data split as Clean: abstract repos + datasources, `UseCase<Params, Result>`, entity vs model.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq architecture "mvc")}}
```text
lib/src/
├── controllers/    # state & orchestration ({{stateManagement}})
├── models/
├── services/       # repositories & API access
├── views/          # screens & widgets
├── routing/
└── theme/
```

**Rules**

- Views only talk to controllers — no direct service calls from widgets.
- Controllers orchestrate services — no Flutter widget imports in controllers.
- One controller per screen or cohesive flow.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq architecture "mvvm")}}
```text
lib/src/
├── ui/             # screens, widgets, state ({{stateManagement}})
├── data/           # models, repository impls
├── routing/
├── services/
└── theme/
```

**Rules**

- UI layer binds to view models / providers / controllers under `ui/`.
- Data access goes through repositories in `data/` or `services/`.
- No business logic in widget `build()` methods.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq architecture "layer-first")}}
```text
lib/src/
├── presentation/   # screens, providers/blocs, widgets
├── domain/         # entities, repo contracts, use cases
├── data/           # models, datasources, repository impls
├── routing/
├── services/
└── theme/
```

**Rules**

- `domain/` has no Flutter or `data/` imports.
- `data/` implements `domain/` contracts only (`AuthRemoteDataSource`, `AuthRepository`).
- Use cases live under `domain/usecases/` and implement `UseCase<Params, Result>`.
- `presentation/` depends on domain abstractions — not concrete datasources.
{{/if}}

## Dart growth patterns (all architectures)

- **Sealed types** for variants: `Failure`, `SessionState`, `RequestState<T>`, auth events/states. Prefer exhaustive `switch` over `if (x is Y)`.
- **Abstract contracts + `implements`**: repositories and datasources hide services/SDKs.
- **Generics**: `FutureEither<T>`, `RequestState<T>`, `UseCase<Params, Result>`.
- **Mixins**: `StreamSubscriptionsMixin` for cancelling stream listeners in notifiers/blocs.
- **Factories**: `AppUser.fromJson` / `Failure.fromException` / `UserModel.toEntity()`.
- **Records**: use for small param bundles (e.g. `LoginParams = ({String email, String password})`).
- Do **not** add Freezed unless the user opts in — language sealed classes are the default.
